description:
In main.rs, the drain loop reads:

  while in_flight_drain.load(Ordering::Acquire) > 0 {
      notify_drain.notified().await;
  }

If the last in-flight connection decrements the counter and calls notify_one() after the load() returns > 0 but before notified().await has registered the waiter, the notification is lost. The drain then blocks until the 10-second timeout fires instead of returning immediately.

The standard fix is to obtain the Notified future BEFORE checking the counter (register first, then check), which avoids the window. The 10-second timeout bounds the worst case so this is not a correctness failure — no data loss, no dropped requests — but it causes unnecessarily slow shutdown on the unlucky race.

Fix: use tokio::sync::Notify::notified() with the register-before-check pattern.
